course: dictionary
lesson: 13800
title: Strong words, strong feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how strong something seems. Invincible means too strong to be beaten. «The knight seemed invincible, and nobody had ever beaten him.» Nobody has won, so invincible means nobody can beat him.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The team had won every game all season, so the fans called them invincible.» Winning every game is the clue that they are very hard to beat. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning, such as "impossible to beat", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Invincible can also describe a feeling, as in «invincible courage», meaning courage so firm that nothing can shake it. A story may call a hero invincible and then show a weak spot. The word tells you what a character believes, and the story tells you what is really true.
fact: Invincible means too strong to be beaten or defeated.
fact: «Invincible» can also mean so firm that nothing can shake it, as in «invincible hope».
fact: In 1588 the Spanish fleet was called the Invincible Armada, but it was still defeated.
fact: People who «feel invincible» may take risks, but no one is invincible on a bike without a helmet.
fact: Useful phrases: «seem invincible», «an invincible team», «invincible courage».
exercise: «The knight seemed invincible, and nobody had ever beaten him.» What does invincible mean here? | *Too strong to be beaten | Lost in the forest | Tired and hungry | Very small and quiet
exercise: «She had invincible courage, and nothing could shake her.» What does invincible describe? | *Courage so firm that nothing can shake it | A loud noise in the night | A cold winter morning | Courage that is very weak
exercise: Ben says, «We feel invincible on our bikes!» Why could this be a safety trap? | Feeling invincible means you cannot fall off | *Nobody is invincible, so a helmet still matters | Helmets are too heavy to wear | Bikes are always fast, so helmets are not needed
test: Which word means too strong to be beaten? | curt | *invincible | barely | glum
test: Which phrase describes a team that nobody can beat? | a drooped smile | *an invincible team | a barely whisper | a curt cough
exam: The story says, «The army seemed invincible, but the walls had a secret gap.» What does the story suggest about invincible? | *The army is not really unbeatable | The walls are invincible | The army is unbeatable forever | The army is very small
